---
title: Get help now
description: >-
  Urgent help if you are in crisis, struggling with pain or your mental health,
  or in money difficulty. Free UK phone numbers, open now.
summary: >-
  If you need help right now, you are not alone. These free services can help,
  many of them at any time of day or night.
lastUpdated: 2026-09-25
---

{% callout type="danger" title="If you or someone else is in immediate danger" %}
Call **999** or go to your nearest A&E. If you cannot speak, call 999 and press 55 when asked, or text 999 if you have registered with the emergencySMS service.
{% /callout %}

## Urgent medical help

- **NHS 111:** call 111 or go to 111.nhs.uk. Free, day or night.
- **Mental health crisis:** call NHS 111 and choose the **mental health option**, in England and Wales.

## Someone to talk to, any time

- **Samaritans:** call free on **116 123**, day or night, or email jo@samaritans.org
- **Shout:** text **SHOUT to 85258** for free, 24 hour text support
- **CALL (Wales):** call free on **0800 132 737**, or text "help" to 81066

## Help with money worries

- **Citizens Advice:** free help with benefits, debt and bills
- **Turn2us:** find benefits and grants you may be entitled to
- **Your local council:** many councils have emergency help for food, energy bills and essentials
- **StepChange:** free debt advice on 0800 138 1111

## Help with pain and long-term conditions

- **Your GP** or **pharmacist**
- **Versus Arthritis helpline:** 0800 5200 520
- **Fibromyalgia Action UK:** support groups and a helpline, at fmauk.org
